CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Advocacy Campaign \n------------------\n\nThis assessment eval
 uates students' ability to apply ethical leadership\, collaborative proble
 m-solving\, and culturally relevant philosophies (like Ubuntu) to real-wor
 ld issues.\n--------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ----------------------------------------\n\n------\nPrompt\n------\n\nAs a
  group\, identify a specific community-based conflict affecting a local co
 mmunity or population group within Africa. Focus on a social\, cultural\, 
 or developmental issue (e.g.\,access to water\, land disputes\, gender-bas
 ed violence\, educational inequality\, or displacement). Choose a conflict
  that allows for ethical leadership\, Ubuntu values\, and community-based 
 collaboration to be meaningfully applied. Then\, develop and present an aw
 areness campaign highlighting and addressing the issue utilising principle
 s of collaboration\, the Ubuntu philosophy\, and ethical values.\n--------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 -----------------------------------------------\n\nThe campaign should out
 line clear objectives and a well-informed strategy on how to solve the pro
 blem. Your deliverable for this task will be a slide deck presentation sho
 wing the selected conflict/problem\, campaign strategy and an implementati
 on plan\, which you will submit and present in a live session as a group. 
 Your presentation should include the following:\n-------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 -------------------------------------------\n\n------------\nIntroduction\
 n------------\n\nProvide a brief overview of the chosen conflict in Africa
 .\nExplain why this issue is significant and needs to be addressed.\nState
  what your campaign aims to achieve and why these goals matter to the affe
 cted community.\n\n---------------------------\nStakeholders Identificatio
 n\n---------------------------\n\nIdentify the key stakeholders involved i
 n or affected by the conflict.\nExplain the role and influence of each sta
 keholder in the context of the conflict.\n\n------------------------------
 --\nApplication of Ubuntu Philosophy\n--------------------------------\n\n
 Demonstrate how principles of Ubuntu (e.g.\, interconnectedness\, compassi
 on\, mutual respect) can be integrated into your campaign.\nProvide specif
 ic examples of how Ubuntu can help transform relationships among stakehold
 ers and promote reconciliation.\n\n--------------------------------\nAppli
 cation of Ethics and Values\n--------------------------------\n\nOutline t
 he core ethical principles and values that will guide the solution you are
  advocating. \n\nMeasuring Success\nPropose methods for evaluating the su
 ccess of your campaign.\nIdentify key performance indicators (KPIs) to tra
 ck progress toward your objectives.\n\nTips for Success\n\nResearch Thorou
 ghly: Understand the historical\, social\, and cultural context of the co
 nflict you choose to address.\nBe Realistic: Set achievable goals and rea
 listic timelines for your campaign activities.\nHighlight Ubuntu: Demonst
 rate how the Ubuntu principles apply to solving the conflict.\n\nRelevant 
 Visuals: Use relevant visuals\, local examples\, or media to enhance your
  storytelling.\nCall to Action: Include calls to action or proposed par
 tnerships (e.g.\, NGOs\, local leaders\, youth groups).\nBe ready to answe
 r the audience’s questions: Anticipate potential obstacles and develop c
 ontingency plans to address them.\n\n \n\n-----------------\nSubmission F
 ormat\n-----------------\n\nPrepare slides for your presentation.\n\nIn ad
 dition to your slide deck\, complete [this team task sheet ] (https://docs
 .google.com/spreadsheets/d/18VwVRsBEMcK0Pom9XZO_NPVsnZknHXHsfyDKVUTpOZ0/ed
 it?gid=0#gid=0)and submit it with the slides. \n\nSubmission and Rubric\n
 \nNaming Format : Assignment Title_Your Name\, example: Advocacy Campaign_
 Group Summative_Cohort 1 Negpod 1\nPresentation time: 10-15 min\nEach memb
 er of the group must present\n\nLinked [here] (https://docs.google.com/spr
 eadsheets/d/1R6m0RM87J_rq8kXWNjXbLnwRIXI_rY3cWcMFwwiTaX4/edit?gid=0#gid=0)
  is the rubric that will be used to assess your work on ALL tasks. Use the
  rubric as a reference for understanding the requirements for excellence a
 s you develop and fine-tune your presentation
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Summative: Awareness Campaign   [_BSE__Self_Leadership_and_Team_Dyn
 amics]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://alueducation.instructure.com/calendar?include_context
 s=course_2815&month=07&year=2026#assignment_39904
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h3><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Ad
 vocacy Campaign&nbsp\;</strong></span></h3>\n<h3><span style="font-size: 1
 2pt\;"><i>This assessment evaluates students' ability to apply ethical lea
 dership\, collaborative problem-solving\, and culturally relevant philosop
 hies (like Ubuntu) to real-world issues.</i></span></h3>\n<h2><span style=
 "font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Prompt</strong></span></h2>\n<h3><span style="
 font-size: 12pt\;">As a group\, identify a specific </span><span style="fo
 nt-size: 12pt\;"><strong>community-based conflict </strong></span><span st
 yle="font-size: 12pt\;">affecting a local community or population group wi
 thin Africa. Focus on a <strong>social</strong>\, <strong>cultural</strong
 >\, or <strong>developmental</strong> issue (e.g.\,access to water\, land 
 disputes\, gender-based violence\, educational inequality\, or displacemen
 t). Choose a conflict that allows for ethical leadership\, Ubuntu values\,
  and community-based collaboration to be meaningfully applied. </span><spa
 n style="font-size: 12pt\;">Then\, develop and present an awareness campai
 gn highlighting and addressing the issue utilising principles of collabora
 tion\, the Ubuntu philosophy\, and ethical values. </span></h3>\n<h3><span
  style="font-size: 12pt\;">The campaign should outline <strong>clear objec
 tives</strong> and a <strong>well-informed strategy</strong> on how to sol
 ve the problem. Your deliverable for this task will be a <strong>slide dec
 k presentation</strong> showing the <strong>selected conflict/problem</str
 ong>\,</span><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"> <strong>campaign strategy</s
 trong> and an <strong>implementation plan</strong>\, which you will submit
  and present in a live session as a group. Your presentation should includ
 e the following:</span></h3>\n<h2><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>
 Introduction</strong></span></h2>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Prov
 ide a brief overview of the chosen conflict in Africa.<br>Explain why this
  issue is significant and needs to be addressed.<br>State what your campai
 gn aims to achieve and why these goals matter to the affected community.</
 span></p>\n<h2><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Stakeholders Identi
 fication</strong></span></h2>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Identify
  the key stakeholders involved in or affected by the conflict.<br>Explain 
 the role and influence of each stakeholder in the context of the conflict.
 </span></p>\n<h2><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Application of Ub
 untu Philosophy</strong></span></h2>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">D
 emonstrate how principles of Ubuntu (e.g.\, interconnectedness\, compassio
 n\, mutual respect) can be integrated into your campaign.<br>Provide speci
 fic examples of how Ubuntu can help transform relationships among stakehol
 ders and promote reconciliation.</span></p>\n<h2><span style="font-size: 1
 2pt\; color: #c71f23\;"><strong>Application of Ethics and Values</strong><
 /span></h2>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Outline the core ethical p
 rinciples and values that will guide the solution you are advocating.&nbsp
 \;<br></span></p>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><span style="color: 
 #c71f23\;"><strong>Measuring Success</strong></span><br>Propose methods fo
 r evaluating the success of your campaign.<br>Identify key performance ind
 icators (KPIs) to track progress toward your objectives.</span></p>\n<p><s
 pan style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Tips for Success</strong></span></p>
 \n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Research Thoroughly:</strong>
 &nbsp\;Understand the historical\, social\, and cultural context of the co
 nflict you choose to address.<br><strong>Be Realistic:</strong>&nbsp\;Set 
 achievable goals and realistic timelines for your campaign activities.<br>
 <strong>Highlight Ubuntu:&nbsp\;</strong>Demonstrate how the Ubuntu princi
 ples apply to solving the conflict.</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-size:
  12pt\;"><strong>Relevant Visuals:</strong>&nbsp\;Use relevant visuals\, l
 ocal examples\, or media to enhance your storytelling.<br><strong>Call to 
 Action:&nbsp\;</strong>Include&nbsp\;calls to action&nbsp\;or proposed par
 tnerships (e.g.\, NGOs\, local leaders\, youth groups).<br><strong>Be read
 y to answer the audience’s questions: </strong>Anticipate potential obst
 acles and develop contingency plans to address them.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp\
 ;</p>\n<h2><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><strong>Submission Format</stro
 ng></span></h2>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Prepare slides for you
 r presentation.</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">In addition
  to your slide deck\, complete <a class="inline_disabled" title="Link" hre
 f="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/18VwVRsBEMcK0Pom9XZO_NPVsnZknHXH
 sfyDKVUTpOZ0/edit?gid=0#gid=0" target="_blank">this team task sheet </a>an
 d submit it with the slides.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-size:
  12pt\;"><strong>Submission and Rubric</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style
 ="font-size: 12pt\;">Naming Format : Assignment Title_Your Name\, example:
  Advocacy Campaign_Group Summative_Cohort 1 Negpod 1<br>Presentation time:
  10-15 min<br>Each member of the group must present</span></p>\n<p><span s
 tyle="font-size: 12pt\;">Linked <a class="inline_disabled" href="https://d
 ocs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1R6m0RM87J_rq8kXWNjXbLnwRIXI_rY3cWcMFwwiTaX4
 /edit?gid=0#gid=0" target="_blank">here</a> is the rubric that will be use
 d to assess your work on ALL tasks. Use the rubric as a reference for unde
 rstanding the requirements for excellence as you develop and fine-tune you
 r presentation</span></p>
